cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these data or scripts, please cite this repository and the
  accompanying article. A version archived with a DOI will follow on
  publication.
type: software
title: >-
  Heine Attribution Studies: Bayesian and Stylometric Authentication
  of Pseudo-Heineana (Case 1: Der Vagabund, 1848)
authors:
  - family-names: auf der Horst
    given-names: Christoph
    affiliation: Heinrich-Heine-Universität Düsseldorf
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9372-7537'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/ch-auf-der-horst/heine-attribution-bayes-stylometry'
abstract: >-
  Data and scripts for assessing the authenticity of texts attributed to
  Heinrich Heine. Case 1 (folder vagabund-1848): texts, scripts, test
  protocols and results for the attribution of ten poems that Enno Hektor
  printed in 1848 in the journal Der Vagabund as poems by Heinrich Heine:
  Bayesian assessment with a reference class and sensitivity analysis,
  calibrated stylometry (Cosine Delta) on short texts.
keywords:
  - Heinrich Heine
  - Pseudo-Heineana
  - authorship attribution
  - Bayesian inference
  - likelihood ratio
  - stylometry
  - Cosine Delta
  - short texts
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - CC-BY-SA-4.0
version: 1.0.0
